  "description": "<p>At the moment, there are no restrictions on use of the \"fcr:\" prefix in URLs of resources on creation.</p>\n\n<p>This request creates a resource named \"fcr:stuff\"</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -XPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/fcr:stuff -v</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>This is different from previous versions of fedora, and can result in creation of resources with names that overlap with reserved endpoints, like \"fcr:tx\". You can create <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/hello/fcr:tx\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/hello/fcr:tx</a></p>",
